                <div class="ow-faq">


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            What is office worker wellness?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                Office worker wellness is the practical
                                support of physical comfort, movement,
                                recovery, stress management and
                                sustainable working for people whose
                                jobs involve significant desk,
                                computer or office-based work.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </details>


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            How can I reduce prolonged sitting at work?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                Interrupt long periods of sitting by
                                standing, walking, changing position
                                and taking brief movement breaks.
                                Adjust your workstation so comfortable
                                movement is possible rather than
                                trying to maintain one position all
                                day.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </details>


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            How often should an office worker take a movement break?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                A practical starting point is a brief
                                two- to three-minute movement
                                interruption approximately once an
                                hour, where the nature of the work
                                allows it.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </details>


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            Is working on a laptop bad for posture?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                Laptop use can encourage downward
                                viewing and a fixed relationship
                                between the screen and keyboard.
                                For prolonged use, a workstation
                                arrangement that allows the screen
                                and input devices to be positioned
                                comfortably may be preferable.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </details>


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            How does Lagos traffic affect office worker wellness?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                A long commute can add another extended
                                period of sitting to a workday that
                                already includes substantial desk work.
                                Treating commuting as part of the
                                overall daily routine can help
                                professionals think more realistically
                                about movement and recovery.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </details>


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            Can massage help office workers relax?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                Massage can be part of a personal
                                relaxation and recovery routine for
                                some people. It should complement
                                appropriate workstation habits and
                                professional healthcare when needed,
                                rather than being presented as a
                                treatment for an underlying medical
                                condition.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </details>


                    <details>

                        <summary>
                            When should I seek professional healthcare?
                        </summary>

                        <div class="ow-faq-answer">

                            <p>
                                Persistent, severe, worsening or
                                concerning symptoms should be assessed
                                by an appropriately qualified
                                healthcare professional. General
                                workplace wellness information should
                                not replace individual medical advice.
                            </p>

                        </div>

